# This CITATION.cff file describes how to cite this software.
# NOTE: fill in the Zenodo DOI of the first release in `identifiers` below.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
title: >-
  baboon-acoustics: supplementary code and materials of
  "On the Reliability of Wahoo Formant Measurements: A Response
  to Boë et al. (2026)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Berthommier
    given-names: Frédéric
    affiliation: "CNRS, Grenoble INP, GIPSA-Lab, Université Grenoble Alpes, Grenoble, France"
    email: frederic.berthommier@gipsa-lab.grenoble-inp.fr
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
    description: Versioned DOI of this deposit (filled after the first Zenodo release)
repository-code: "https://github.com/FBerthommier/baboon-acoustics"
url: "https://fberthommier.github.io/baboon-acoustics/"
abstract: >-
  Supplementary code and materials of the article "On the Reliability of
  Wahoo Formant Measurements: A Response to Boë et al. (2026)"
  (International Journal of Primatology, 2026). Contains the complete
  supplementary document, all figures, the original analysis scripts
  archived verbatim, and a refactored Python package (baboon_acoustics)
  for formant tracking with Praat's Burg method and with iterative
  adaptive inverse filtering (IAIF), fundamental-frequency estimation
  including a Gaussian pre-filtered autocorrelation mode,
  vocal-tract-length estimation after Reby & McComb (2003), and
  glottal-source analysis (single pulse and full pulse train), with
  figure-reproduction scripts, a guided example, interactive HTML demos,
  unit tests and a compiled user documentation.
keywords:
  - bioacoustics
  - formants
  - vocal tract length
  - fundamental frequency
  - IAIF
  - Praat
  - Parselmouth
  - baboon
license: MIT
